  "fixture_manifest_sha256": "e2d177e5b8fec74d7e348f731008868b558ce95f39eb0e3b93ea3cfa5ab169d7",
  "notes": {
    "build_strategy": "Build once into repo/_output/net10.0/linux-x64/publish with UI beside the launcher. Snapshot publish including publish/UI and record head.txt under /workspace/tmp/linux-program-build-output. Later stages reuse that output. Source libraries stay read-only; fixtures are approved disposable copies.",
    "known_product_blocker": "Prior exact-head evidence (acceptance-stages/t_e53b844e) recorded a linux-x64 startup crash (FileNotFoundException: Microsoft.Extensions.Primitives v10.0.0.0 at Bootstrap.GetConfiguration) at head fa61fc55. The build stage re-verifies the Primitives DLL in this candidate's publish output (B2) with startup proof as the primary assertion. If that product/build defect is still present at this candidate, the build stage startup proof and all dependent stages will fail; that requirement is recorded, not waived, and no product code is rewritten here.",
    "placeholders": "task_id/head_sha use @TASK@/@HEAD@; case-owned fresh writable data uses @CASE@ (materialized to acceptance-stages/<task>/data).",
    "repair_input_generalization": "Corrections from linux-program-repair-input/manifest.json (case 60354f1854f5483c56e6b0d1, task t_dd7ab58b at fa61fc55) are generalized into this reusable template: provider-enablement wire names are camelCase (enableOpenLibraryProvider/enableHardcoverFallback/hardcoverApiToken) with the id=1 guard and the hard-fail after failed enablement; I3 targets /api/v1/metadata/providers/health/basic and I4 targets /api/v1/metadata/providers/health (both rows carry providerName; the bare /metadata/providers base route has no [HttpGet] action and is not a definitions endpoint); search terms are URL-quoted; the browser check verifies that the login route serves the packaged top-level UI/login.html with its antiforgery token applied. The case-owned start_app.sh corrections (reviewed, t_d325f8e1/t_dd7ab58b) were already generalized: per-case DATA_DIR/APP_PORT bindings, durable _output/net10.0/linux-x64/publish + UI, bind-address 127.0.0.1 and ASPNETCORE_URLS, and no secret values in the launcher.",
    "scope": "Reusable Linux acceptance program for Swartdraak/Bibliophilarr; the registered candidate is c3a458a464301890bfd5d4e3231e0f7e7fe04b2f (source: fix(issue-426) duplicate-copy import record preservation). The harness reads the expected source head from runner-owned ONYX_STAGE_HEAD and never hardcodes a candidate SHA into executable files. Shared behavior on Linux; native Windows/macOS smoke is a separate platform stage and is out of scope here.",
    "secrets": "No secret values are stored in this program. Credentials are projected at execution time through the runner secret_env broker (SIXLABORS_LICENSE_KEY -> SIXLABORS_LICENSE_FILE env var for the backend build via secret_file_env, a private byte-exact 0600 file whose PATH is bound to the MSBuild-recognized SIXLABORS_LICENSE_FILE variable per src/Directory.Build.props; removed on cleanup; HARDCOVER_API_KEY -> BIBLIOPHILARR_HARDCOVER_API_TOKEN env var for the integrations/workflows check steps, where it is persisted as the DB hardcoverApiToken by the provider-enablement helper). The app service itself starts with no provider secrets; provider enablement happens through the authenticated config API.",
    "browser_runtime": "Pre-provision the pinned Playwright Python dependency from tests/browser/requirements.txt and Chromium plus its system dependencies on the browser runner. The checks import the repository login helper, use only the disposable loopback app, and store only a prior process-start timestamp between the two steps."
  },
